<title>POLAND: BWR plans 50 pct 1996 dividend payout.</title>
<headline>BWR plans 50 pct 1996 dividend payout.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish Bank Wspolpracy Regionalnej SA (BWR) has earmarked 2.3 million zlotys of its 4.6-million-zloty 1996 net profit for dividend, the bank said in a statement on Tuesday.</p>
<p>BWR said the management's proposal would be voted on at the bank's general shareholders meeting on June 11.</p>
<p>It said the remaining funds would be earmarked for reserves, a risk fund and for bonuses for supervisory board and management's members. -- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
